message: "If you use this archive, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LIFELINE preliminary evidence: a derived aggregation-core congruence and a leave transition generated from a change rule in MetaTensor"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Izawa
    given-names: Yusuke
    affiliation: Tokyo Metropolitan University
abstract: >-
  Preliminary evidence for the ERC proposal LIFELINE. (A) A stand-alone model
  of an aggregation core derives, from declared promises alone, the coarsest
  partition of histories that a later change can tell apart (79 classes for an
  order-dependent promise, 9 otherwise, over all histories of up to three
  steps), confirmed by exhaustive search and by a separately written
  certificate checker. Lean 4 proofs cover the order-independent case for
  histories of any length. (B) In MetaTensor, a 7-line change rule
  leave(p, reason) is compiled by the meta-tracer. The archived run data and
  scripts re-derive
  its agreement with an independent checker on five histories and its 1.16
  GPU launches per step against 5.00 for a hand-written adapter.
keywords:
  - meta-tracing
  - dynamic reconfiguration
  - program transformation
  - compositional congruence
  - GPU
